-- title:
--   Regularity of the pole chart of the Igusa special fibre
-- statement:
--   Fix an integer $N \ge 1$ and a prime $\ell$ with $\ell \nmid N$, and write $\mathbb{Z}_{(\ell)}$ for the subring [`GaloisRep.ratLocalizedAt`](def/GaloisRep_Flat.html#L8) $\ell$ of $\mathbb{Q}$ consisting of those rationals whose denominator is coprime to $\ell$. Let $k$ be an algebraically closed field of characteristic $\ell$, equipped with a $\mathbb{Z}_{(\ell)}$-algebra structure. Let $A =$ `chartAlgInf` $N$ $\ell$ be the $\mathbb{Z}_{(\ell)}$-subalgebra of the full modular function field $F =$ `modularFunctionFieldFull` $N$ consisting of the elements of $F$ that are integral over the $\mathbb{Z}_{(\ell)}$-subalgebra generated by $j^{-1}$, where $j$ is the element `jFull` $N$ of $F$; that is, $A$ is the integral closure of $\mathbb{Z}_{(\ell)}[j^{-1}]$ in $F$. Then for every maximal ideal $\mathfrak{m}$ of the base-changed ring $k \otimes_{\mathbb{Z}_{(\ell)}} A$, the localisation $(k \otimes_{\mathbb{Z}_{(\ell)}} A)_{\mathfrak{m}}$ is a regular local ring and its Krull dimension, as an element of $\mathbb{N}_\infty$, equals $1$.
--
--   This is the ring-theoretic form, on the chart around the cusp $j = \infty$, of Igusa's theorem on good reduction of modular curves at primes not dividing the level: the special fibre of the chart is regular of dimension one at each of its closed points. It feeds the statement that the corresponding chart of the Igusa scheme becomes smooth of relative dimension one after passing to the residue field, via [`ModularCurve.IgusaScheme.smoothOfRelativeDimension_one_pullback_chartInf_residue`](thm.html#ModularCurve.IgusaScheme.smoothOfRelativeDimension_one_pullback_chartInf_residue).
